WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.990
In 1992 to 93, about 6,700
passengers landed in Antarctica.

2
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:11.410
Now, over 100,000 people visit each year.

3
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.410
About 98 per cent of tourist
voyages head to one place:

4
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.350
the Antarctic Peninsula.

5
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.890
And Antarctica is fragile.

6
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.070
In the cold, damage lasts a long time.

7
00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.490
So who decides how to keep it wild?

8
00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.950
Or does nobody make the rules at all?

9
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.790
In this mission, you'll see what
makes Antarctica a wilderness,

10
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.970
and what puts it under pressure.

11
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.930
Then you'll follow a
timeline of decisions,

12
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.470
and test the rules on landings.

13
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:42.760
Your mission: find out who decides
how Antarctica is protected.
